    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Slowest express orders, last hour",
      "description": "The ten express orders of the last hour with the longest elapsed time (closed orders sort last).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
        "uid": "fs-postgres"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
            "uid": "fs-postgres"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT coalesce(s.store_name, o.store_id) AS \"store\", o.order_id AS \"order\", promised_minutes AS \"promise (min)\", CASE WHEN delivered_at IS NULL AND closed_without_delivery THEN NULL ELSE round((EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (coalesce(delivered_at, now()) - created_at)) / 60.0)::numeric, 1) END AS \"elapsed (min)\", CASE WHEN delivered_at IS NULL AND closed_without_delivery THEN 'closed without delivery' WHEN ((delivered_at IS NOT NULL AND delivered_at - created_at > promised_minutes * interval '1 minute') OR (delivered_at IS NULL AND NOT closed_without_delivery AND now() - created_at > promised_minutes * interval '1 minute' + interval '1 minute')) THEN 'breached' WHEN delivered_at IS NULL AND now() - created_at >= promised_minutes * interval '45 seconds' THEN 'at risk' ELSE 'on time' END AS \"state\" FROM live_express_orders o LEFT JOIN dim_store s ON s.store_id = o.store_id WHERE created_at >= now() - interval '1 hour' ORDER BY 4 DESC NULLS LAST, o.order_id LIMIT 10"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Express definitions",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**On time**: delivered within the order's own promise (`delivered_at - created_at <= promised_minutes`). **Breached**: delivered later than the promise, or still undelivered more than the promise plus a 1-minute grace after it was created (the grace keeps a `delivered` event that reaches the sink a batch late from raising a false alarm). **At risk**: undelivered and at least 75% of the promise has passed (15 minutes for a 20-minute promise), not yet breached. An order that was cancelled or returned without a delivery is **closed without delivery**: it has no delivery to be late, so it is in no count. Times are simulator event times; the state is computed with now(), so it moves between Silver batches."
      }
    }
  ]
}
